{"kind":"pr","url":"https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/49006","repo":"huggingface/transformers","number":49006,"set":"human","title":"Fix mps autocast handling in rotary embeddings","body":"<!-- ci-dashboard-badge:start -->\n[![CPU CI](https://transformers-ci.lor-e.huggingface.cool/badge/pr?pr=49006&event=pr-ci)](https://transformers-ci.lor-e.huggingface.cool/d/pytest-observability-by-pr/pytest-observability-branch?var-pr=49006) [![GPU run-slow](https://transformers-ci.lor-e.huggingface.cool/badge/pr?pr=49006&event=run-slow)](https://transformers-ci.lor-e.huggingface.cool/d/pytest-observability-by-pr/pytest-observability-branch?var-pr=49006)\n<!-- ci-dashboard-badge:end -->\n\n# What does this PR do?\r\n\r\nCPU fallback was added in [#29439](https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/29439) because at that time autocast wasn't supported on MPS. \r\n\r\nPyTorch added support in [2.5](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/releases/tag/v2.5.0) for MPS for this. This PR removes the workaround so RoPE calculations correctly remain float32 inside MPS autocast contexts.","authorType":"User","additions":216,"deletions":216,"changedFiles":193,"files":[{"path":"src/transformers/models/afmoe/modeling_afmoe.py","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/transformers/models/apertus/modeling_apertus.py","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/transformers/models/arcee/modeling_arcee.py","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/transformers/models/aria/modeling_aria.py","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/transformers/models/axk1/modeling_axk1.py","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/transformers/models/axk2/modeling_axk2.py","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/transformers/models/bamba/modeling_bamba.py","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/transformers/models/bitnet/modeling_bitnet.py","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/transformers/models/blt/modeling_blt.py","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/transformers/models/blt/modula